error[E0277]: `i64` is not a valid value here: this attribute takes a `StringValue`
 --> tests/compile_errors/17_typed_literal_wrong_type.rs:7:32
  |
7 |     event!(shop.order.placed { shop.order.id: 5i64, shop.cart.item_count: 1 });
  |                                ----^^^^^^^^^
  |                                |
  |                                expected a `StringValue`
  |                                required by a bound introduced by this call
  |
  = note: `StringValue`: `&str`, `&String`, `String`, `Cow<'static, str>`, `Arc<str>` | `IntValue`: any integer up to 64 bits (`u64`/`usize` saturate at `i64::MAX`) | `DoubleValue`: `f64`, `f32` | `BoolValue`: `bool` | arrays: `Vec<…>` of those | enums: the enum, a string literal, or `custom(…)` | `Pii<…>` (`sensitivity: pii`): wrap the value in `redacted(…)` or `hashed(…)` | `Typed<K, T>` (`code_generation.rust.type`): pass a `T`
help: the trait `IntoValue<StringValue>` is not implemented for `i64`
      but trait `IntoValue<IntValue>` is implemented for it
 --> $WORKSPACE/crates/semlex/src/lib.rs
